  "id": "DrugBank_DB00227 - MONDO_5347",
  "verbalization": "Lovastatin, through its indication for Familial Hyperlipidemia and Hyperlipidemia, Familial Combined, and Lpl Related conditions, appears to be linked to Hypertriglyceridemia (disease) via a chain of indications. The evidence suggests that Lovastatin may influence lipid metabolism, potentially reducing triglyceride levels, which could contribute to the development of hypertriglyceridemia. This pathway is supported by the indirect relationship between Lovastatin and Ciprofibrate, which in turn is associated with Hypertriglyceridemia, indicating a possible role of Ciprofibrate in the pathophysiology of the disease. The integration of these indications highlights a potential mechanism by which Lovastatin may be repurposed to address hypertriglyceridemia, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
